{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "הוסר", :translit "husar", :gloss "it is removed"} {:he "חלב", :translit "chelev", :gloss "fat"} {:he "ומעת הוסר התמיד", :translit "u'meat husar ha-tamid", :gloss "and from the time the daily offering is removed"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "הוסר", :b "חלב"}], :frame {:text "The daily offering (tamid) was slaughtered and its parts prepared on the altar; once its sacrificial service was completed, the time for eating the remaining offerings and consecrated foods would arrive, signaling the suspension of restriction (hatarah). The phrase 'from the time the daily offering was removed' is used in tractate Pesachim to determine the latest time for eating chametz on erev Pesach, since that is when the tamid's processing concludes. The Ba'al HaTurim links this to the verse 'it is removed' (Leviticus 4:31) via gematria with 'fat,' suggesting that once the tamid is offered, all fat — representing the substance and nourishment of the world — becomes accessible, because blessing flows into creation through the merit of the tamid's sacrifice.", :sources ["Pesachim 20a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "הוסר", :a-value 271, :b "חלב", :b-value 40, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:22:04.684064014Z", :model "glm-5.2"}